## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Vite + React project.

### Changes Made

**Files Modified:**

1. **package.json** - Added `@vercel/speed-insights` dependency
   - Installed version: Latest compatible version from npm registry

2. **package-lock.json** - Updated lockfile with new dependency
   - Ensures consistent dependency resolution across environments

3. **src/App.tsx** - Integrated SpeedInsights component
   - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/react";`
   - Added component to JSX: `<SpeedInsights />` within the TooltipProvider, after Toaster components
   - Placement ensures Speed Insights runs on all pages while maintaining existing app structure

### Implementation Details

- **Framework**: React with Vite (identified from package.json and vite.config.ts)
- **Integration Method**: Used the React-specific package export (`@vercel/speed-insights/react`) as per official Vercel documentation
- **Component Placement**: Added at the app root level to track all routes and page transitions
- **Documentation Source**: Fetched latest instructions from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart

### Verification Steps Completed

✅ **Build**: Project builds successfully with no compilation errors
✅ **Linter**: No new linting errors introduced in modified files
✅ **Tests**: All 102 tests pass (18 test files)
✅ **Lock Files**: package-lock.json properly updated with new dependency

### Next Steps

To start collecting Speed Insights data:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for this project
3. Visit your deployed site to start tracking performance metrics

The Speed Insights tracking script will automatically collect Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, FCP, TTFB, INP) and send them to Vercel for analysis.
